WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.889
Film Courage: What do you recommend to a writer
that is too much of a perfectionist?

00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:06.510
And on the flip side maybe one who is too
loose and maybe a little sloppy?

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.130
Daniel Calvisi, movie studio reader, screenwriter
and private screenplay consultant: If you’re

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:13.280
too much of a perfectionist you need to understand
that you need to get it out of the door at

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.150
a certain point or drop that script and move
on to another.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.480
A writer writes, they write more than one
script.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.930
You can’t obsess over the same script for
years.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.080
I’ve done it, everybody has done it.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.560
It’s your baby and you want it to be perfect.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.320
It’s good that you want to be super detail-oriented
and you want it to be of a high quality level

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.420
and not have any typos or spelling errors
and really blow away the readers.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.590
So it’s going to take away some time to
write.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:44.890
It’s going to take years to write that great
breakthrough script but you have to get it

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.170
out the door at some point or drop it and
move on.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:53.500
So if you’re planning to get it out the
door then you have to cut it off at some point

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:00.960
and say “I’m going to submit this to a
contest or a manager or a producer or whoever

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.920
and it’s tough to get it out the door because
you’re never sure if it’s exactly ready.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.219
But it’s probably never going to be perfect.

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:16.499
It’s probably never going to be the exact
submission ready level that that needs to

00:01:16.499 --> 00:01:17.889
be.

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:25.240
It’s subjective to the reader so it’s
hard to say “Okay, this is absolutely where

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:28.680
you should cut it off and you should send
it out the door.”

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.130
It’s your choice and it’s one of the toughest
choices for writers when do you submit?

